build progress endpoint, which is silence rather than error, and I have not extended them here because this head is scoped to anchors.\n\nWhat this deliberately does not do. Five pages still rest on retired artifacts at path dot — gs/status.md, mcp/status.md and mcp/wait.md on b3837885, mcp/work.md and mcp/inspect.md on 00421fa7. Those cannot be repaired by choosing a successor, because dot carries about fifty-five live artifacts and selecting one would invent a provenance rather than repair one. That is the dot-artifact migration, which AGENTS.md says takes its own request and a ratifier to run. Narrowing is recorded as an assert on the promise rather than left as a silent shortfall.\n\nThe four page-level artifacts are not retired here. The wider docs path is the declared winner over them and retiring them is a merge-step act.\n\nThe docset gates pass, including the executable examples; git diff --check is clean; the worktree is clean; the head is zero commits behind main and merges clean.","body":{"branch":"request/doc-anchor-repair","commit":"c4939b98e905dcb03de0b4a9778b9dfa6f5f15e1","head":"c4939b98e905dcb03de0b4a9778b9dfa6f5f15e1","path":"docs"}}